From d79ab6b6f415c5588894fb68b0778248936647be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: J P <1953637+jpwatters@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:43:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 48/54] README: setup picture with the optional FTDI remote
 power-on

The setup picture (docs/nas/qmx-nas-setup.png) now shows the optional
PC817 opto board on the QMX+ power-on pins, driven from the NAS by an FTDI
TTL-232R-5V cable (Remote Power-ON, patch 0047), next to the QMX+ on USB,
the Synology DS416j, the Ubiquiti switch and the Tab5 on Wi-Fi or the
optional W5500 PoE base. The alt text says the same.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W7MAsxUnuCnfwkHxdqp61S
---
 README.md                  |   2 +-
 docs/nas/qmx-nas-setup.png | Bin 203112 -> 316974 bytes
 2 files changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 05971ea2..80304153 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@ Each new upstream release can stop the patches applying: new settings take the s
 | v2.0.2 (2026-11-18) | Upstream took bits 161 (RTTY contest) and 162 (TX subnet interlock); the README’s licence section, where the NAS appendix follows, changed; the web radio’s MP3 decoder was replaced | Relay setting bit 163; the appendix kept after upstream’s new licence text; nothing to carry for the MP3 decoder |
 | v2.1.0 (2026-11-22) | No conflicting change, but the patches added on the Mac since v2.0.2 could not be merged by the kit, which had no matching base to merge from | Series rebased onto v2.1.0; the "TX locked" refusals use upstream’s new red alert toast |
 
-<p align="center"><img src="docs/nas/qmx-nas-setup.png" alt="QRP Labs QMX+ connected by USB to a Synology DS416j NAS, wired to a Ubiquiti 8-port switch on the LAN; an M5Stack Tab5 joins either by Wi-Fi or by Ethernet through the optional W5500 PoE base on switch port 1" width="600"></p>
+<p align="center"><img src="docs/nas/qmx-nas-setup.png" alt="QRP Labs QMX+ connected by USB to a Synology DS416j NAS, with an optional PC817 opto board on the QMX+ power-on pins driven from the NAS by an FTDI TTL-232R-5V cable; the NAS is wired to a Ubiquiti 8-port switch on the LAN; an M5Stack Tab5 joins either by Wi-Fi or by Ethernet through the optional W5500 PoE base on switch port 1" width="600"></p>
 
 Here’s what the QMX+ PanadapterShared adds on top of upstream QMX-Panadapter, with how far each has been tested:
 1. Sharing the radio over the network (Synology NAS or Raspberry Pi relay)
